  Entries:
  - Id: note-a
    Title: Watch orders
    Body: 'Before dark, make the rounds: radio, vane, shore and woods. Tick each off in the watch book. Rest indoors after nightfall. If you hear footsteps following yours, shut the door behind you.'
  - Id: note-b
    Title: Rubbing notes from the last watch
    Body: "Start at the upper right and follow the shallow groove. Three stones often sit in a row. The mark on the right stays the same; the notches on the left change. In my book I pencilled \u201Cday\u201D beside the mark.\n\nWhen that day comes, look at the row below. Sketch the weather vane and hold it beside the cut in the stone. Leave doubtful marks blank. Fill them in on tomorrow's rounds."
  - Id: flashlight
    Title: Torch
    Body: One press for light. Press again to go dark.
  - Id: note-t1
    Title: Loose leaf I
    Body: On the third day it shall move.
  - Id: note-t2
    Title: Loose leaf II
    Body: On the fifth day it shall have a voice.
  - Id: note-t3
    Title: Loose leaf III
    Body: On the seventh day it shall have light.
  - Id: note-t4
    Title: Loose leaf IV
    Body: On the ninth day it shall have flesh.
  - Id: note-t5
    Title: Bell keeper's note
    Body: When a bell rings, remember the direction. It has just entered that part of the wood. If it stands still, the bell falls silent too.
  - Id: T07
    Title: The last tablet
    Body: The corner has broken away. The notch in the empty cabin stand would fit that edge.
  NightHour: 18
  Opening: Alone at the snow station. Make your rounds and keep the watch until relief arrives. Tab opens the watch book.
